        {
          "paragraph": 31,
          "source_lines": [
            110,
            110
          ],
          "translation_lines": [
            110,
            110
          ],
          "source_characters": 35,
          "translation_characters": 13,
          "unchanged": false,
          "source_sha256": "090a6f9a69bb99a8d502468764c79a960b9f34f79dca6068e493a5af77bde776",
          "translation_sha256": "ef763ab6fb3b42ef78d254f47fe8b431bb7269ea9c731ab3d428861cbfb4c0a1",
          "source_text": "## Node-stage relation obligations\n",
          "translation_text": "## 节点阶段的关系义务\n"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 32,
          "source_lines": [
            112,
            112
          ],
          "translation_lines": [
            112,
            112
          ],
          "source_characters": 670,
          "translation_characters": 302,
          "unchanged": false,
          "source_sha256": "ce586449295b71e1efd5b72926f35974a25f0fde0a027553638e42bfe019520a",
          "translation_sha256": "0bd07897bf6a8e8e8a45f5b6de9b99c07b6285cbb81cd93c89b279dfe99b80a0",
          "source_text": "A `node_relation_followup`, `node_relation_obligations` envelope (including its diagnostics/relation_followups), or `structural_diagnostics` entry is a required preservation outcome, not an optional inspection signal. Read its original relation records and original-to-current ID mapping; a retired ID alone does not prove its knowledge was removed or may be discarded. Close every supplied obligation using the accepted node content as the baseline, preserving valid roles, paired meanings, provenance and branch scope. Do not reopen node definitions merely to avoid representing their relations. If node content itself is defective, state the concrete counterexample.\n",
          "translation_text": "`node_relation_followup`、`node_relation_obligations` 输入封装（包括其中的 diagnostics/relation_followups），或 `structural_diagnostics` 条目，都是必须完成的保义结果要求，不是可选的检查信号。读取其原始关系记录及原始 ID 到当前 ID 的映射；仅凭某个 ID 已退役，不能证明其知识已经被移除，也不能证明可以丢弃该知识。以已接受的节点内容为基线，完成每一项给定义务，保留有效角色、配对含义、来源与分支作用域。不得仅为避免表达节点关系而重新审议节点定义。如果节点内容本身有缺陷，应指出具体反例。\n"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 33,
          "source_lines": [
            114,
            114
          ],
          "translation_lines": [
            114,
            114
          ],
          "source_characters": 482,
          "translation_characters": 208,
          "unchanged": false,
          "source_sha256": "b51e8f1dee9b9b933b1c7bf5cd44df99cea05ef07434435628a3a74949da06cc",
          "translation_sha256": "3af3e0580ebb6d052e0314ab2ce42c9860bd956d66bd2c805debe4052ba1b0c0",
          "source_text": "ID rewiring and exact duplicate removal are mechanical. Distinct endpoints whose identity has not been confirmed remain distinct. `properties.alternative_ids` restricts the source owner's branches; it cannot select a target node's alternative. New alternatives do not automatically inherit old version-specific assertions. The independent Graph Assessment must verify each required outcome even when the Writer proposes no edit; a no-op is not proof that an obligation is resolved.\n",
          "translation_text": "ID 重定向与完全重复项的删除属于机械处理。尚未确认同一身份的不同端点仍保持不同。`properties.alternative_ids` 限定起点 owner 的分支，不能选择终点节点的某个 alternative。新增 alternatives 不会自动继承仅属于旧版本的断言。即使 Writer 没有提出修改，独立 Graph Assessment 也必须核查每一项要求的结果；无操作不证明某项义务已经解决。\n"
        }
      ]
    },
